{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.HeisenbergCommutatorProp","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.HeisenbergCommutatorProp","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.hbarQ_maximal_uncertainty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.hbarQ_maximal_uncertainty","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/heisenberg-commutator-prop.lean#L91-L96","doc":"Maximal-uncertainty limit: as `q → ∞` the inverse `q⁻¹ → 0`, so\n`ℏ_q → 1`.  Stated at the formal limit point `u = 0` of the inverse\nparameter, where it is an evaluation of `hbarOfInv` over the base ring —\nno inverse, and no `0⁻¹ = 0` convention, is involved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.heisenberg_commutator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.heisenberg_commutator","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/heisenberg-commutator-prop.lean#L71-L89","doc":"The q-deformed Heisenberg commutator relation:\n`[X, P]_q = J · ℏ_q(p)` where `ℏ_q = 1 - q⁻¹`.\n\nThis captures the structural content of the commutator on the\nfibre `P¹(ℂ)`, where `J` is the complex structure on the Levi\ndistribution (`J² = -Id`) and `q` is the substrate parameter.\nEncoded over a commutative ring with `q` a unit, the commutator is `J`\nscaled by the q-Planck constant `ℏ_q(q) = 1 - q⁻¹`, so the statement\nreduces to the definition of `hbarQ`.\n\nThe full categorical proof — that this scalar relation lifts to\nthe q-deformed operator algebra on the state bundle, via the\ncategorical connection and the Levi distribution structure —\nrequires machinery beyond this scalar fibre statement. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:heisenberg-commutator","label":"prop:heisenberg-commutator","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/heisenberg-commutator-prop.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.hbarQ_classical_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.hbarQ_classical_limit","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/heisenberg-commutator-prop.lean#L67-L69","doc":"Classical limit: as q → 1, the q-Planck constant vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/heisenberg-commutator-prop.lean#L61-L65","doc":"The q-deformed Planck constant: `ℏ_q = 1 - q⁻¹`, for a substrate parameter\ncarried as a unit `q : Rˣ`.\nClassical limit: q → 1 gives ℏ_q → 0.\nMaximal uncertainty: q → ∞ gives ℏ_q → 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.hbarOfInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.hbarOfInv","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/heisenberg-commutator-prop.lean#L53-L59","doc":"The q-Planck constant **as a function of the inverse parameter** `u = q⁻¹`:\n`ℏ = 1 − u`.\n\nCarrying `u` instead of forming `q⁻¹` keeps this division-free over a\ncommutative ring (§7c) and makes each limit point an ordinary evaluation\nrather than an appeal to a junk-value convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/heisenberg-commutator-prop.lean#L46-L47","doc":"The inverse parameter `q⁻¹` as the Laurent monomial `T (-1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.q_param","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/heisenberg-commutator-prop.lean#L44-L45","doc":"The substrate parameter `q` as the Laurent monomial `T 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.R_q","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/heisenberg-commutator-prop.lean#L41-L43","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}